> (define notes (buffers:make "notes" "(harpo:squeeze 3) harpo:honk files:find-file\n"))
> (layout:switch-to-buffer notes)
> (modes:set-major-mode harpo:mode notes)
> (define (describe name) (in-client (lambda () (help:describe-name name (view)))) (help))
; A command: its module, the keys that run it in the view, the modes it
; is marked for, its documentation, and each name a link.
> (in-client (lambda () (help:describe-command files:find-file (view))))
> (help)
# files:find-file
<files:find-file> is a command in (files).
It is on [C-x C-f].
Visits PATH and shows its buffer in the selected view.
> (describe 'harpo:honk)
# harpo:honk
<harpo:honk> is a command in (harpo).
It is on [C-c h].
It is for <harpo:mode>.
Honks once.
> (describe 'harpo:quiet)
# harpo:quiet
<harpo:quiet> is a command in (harpo).
It is on no key; run it with [M-x] harpo:quiet.
It is for no mode.
Does nothing, on no key.
; A command the REPL defines has no module.
> (commands:define-command (bonk) "Bonks." (void))
> (in-client (lambda () (help:describe-command bonk (view))))
> (help)
# bonk
<bonk> is a command of the configuration or the REPL.
It is on no key; run it with [M-x] bonk.
No documentation.
; An option: its value in the view, its setting, its default, and each
; module's setting.
> (describe 'harpo:volume)
# harpo:volume
An option in (harpo).
Its value here is 3; its setting is 3 and its default 3.
How loud a honk is.
> (set-option! harpo:volume 7)
> (buffers:with-buffer notes (set-option-local! harpo:volume 9))
> (describe 'harpo:volume)
# harpo:volume
An option in (harpo).
Its value here is 9; its setting is 7 and its default 3.
## Settings
(repl) sets it to 7.
How loud a honk is.
; A hook or a table: its documentation and how many entries it has.
> (add-hook! harpo:after-honk (lambda () 1))
> (table-set! harpo:horns "bulb" "honk")
> (table-set! harpo:horns "bell" "ding")
> (describe 'harpo:after-honk)
# harpo:after-honk
A hook in (harpo) with 1 entry.
Called after each honk.
> (describe 'harpo:horns)
# harpo:horns
A table in (harpo) with 2 entries.
Maps a horn's name to its sound.
; Saved data: its value.
> (set-saved! harpo:honks 4)
> (describe 'harpo:honks)
# harpo:honks
Saved data in (harpo).
Its value is 4.
; Any other procedure: its documentation; any other value, as write
; prints it; syntax keeps no documentation.
> (describe 'harpo:squeeze)
# harpo:squeeze
A procedure in (harpo).
Squeezes the horn N times.
> (describe 'harpo:mode)
# harpo:mode
A value in (harpo).
Its value is harpo:mode.
> (describe 'harpo:with-horn)
# harpo:with-horn
Syntax in (harpo), which keeps no documentation.
; Tuna's own libraries' names.
> (describe 'set-option!)
# set-option!
A procedure in (tuna).
No documentation.
> (describe 'use-plugin)
# use-plugin
Syntax in (tuna plugins), which keeps no documentation.
> (describe 'eval-text)
# eval-text
A procedure in (tuna eval).
No documentation.
; The overrides and advice on a changeable definition follow, newest
; first, with the module that made each.
> (describe 'report)
# report
A procedure in (tuna).
No documentation.
## Changes
Advice by (echo-area)
> (set! harpo:squeeze (lambda (n) 0))
> (advice-add! harpo:squeeze (lambda (s n) (s n)))
> (describe 'harpo:squeeze)
# harpo:squeeze
A procedure in (harpo).
Squeezes the horn N times.
## Changes
Advice by (repl)
Override by (repl)
; Arguments are checked; a name no loaded module exports is refused,
; such as one the REPL defines.
> (raised (lambda () (help:describe-name 'nothere:x (view))))
(help:describe-name "not an exported name")
> (raised (lambda () (help:describe-name 'bonk (view))))
(help:describe-name "not an exported name")
> (raised (lambda () (help:describe-name "harpo:honk" (view))))
(help:describe-name "not a symbol")
> (raised (lambda () (help:describe-name 'harpo:honk 'x)))
(help:describe-name "not a view")
> (raised (lambda () (help:describe-command 'x (view))))
(help:describe-command "not a command")
; Run by a key, C-h f, C-h v and C-h o read a name, the name at point
; first; C-h x and C-h a read a command, the command at point first.
> (views:set-point! (view) 3)
> (start! "C-h" "f")
> (press! "RET")
> (settle)
> (title)
"harpo:squeeze"
> (start! "C-h" "v")
> (type! "harpo:pitch")
> (press! "RET")
> (settle)
> (title)
"harpo:pitch"
> (views:set-point! (view) 22)
> (start! "C-h" "x")
> (press! "RET")
> (settle)
> (title)
"harpo:honk"
> (start! "C-h" "a")
> (type! "harpo:quiet")
> (press! "RET")
> (settle)
> (title)
"harpo:quiet"
